a as a primary explanation."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Other Hypercalcemia (Drug/Endocrine/Immobilization)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.1834862385321101, "posterior": 0.3656144384416061, "danger": 0.2, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Antacid use for GERD introduces a plausible alternative mechanism (milk-alkali syndrome) that could explain hypercalcemia and elevated alkaline phosphatase."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.1, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["primary hyperparathyroidism", "humoral hypercalcemia of malignancy", "milk-alkali syndrome", "sarcoidosis"]}, "kb_pth_mediated_parathyroid": {"id": "kb_pth_mediated_parathyroid", "label": "PTH-mediated (parathyroid)", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.0, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}}, "frontier": ["B2", "B4"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the combination of subacute systemic symptoms, constitutional signs (weight loss, trouble focusing), and hypercalcemia argue for malignancy-associated hypercalcemia over other causes?", "summary": "The presence of constitutional symptoms (weight loss, neurological changes) and systemic involvement supports malignancy-associated hypercalcemia as a higher-probability cause compared to other hypercalcemia categories."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the patient's antacid use for GERD provide mechanistic support for milk-alkali syndrome as an alternative hypercalcemia cause?", "summary": "Antacid use for GERD introduces a plausible alternative mechanism (milk-alkali syndrome) that could explain hypercalcemia and el